data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"Factor $\\Sigma = LL^\\top$ with `np.linalg.cholesky`. Then $\\log\\det\\Sigma = 2\\sum_i \\log L_{ii}$, and\n$(x-\\mu)^\\top\\Sigma^{-1}(x-\\mu) = \\lVert z\\rVert^2$ where $Lz = x-\\mu$. Check symmetry and positive\ndefiniteness before factoring: `np.linalg.cholesky` raises `LinAlgError` for a matrix that is not\npositive definite, and it silently reads only one triangle when the matrix is asymmetric."},"hints_note":null}

